        "[feite] inheemse naam: 'n Naam uit die taal van mense wat al eeue la — corrected: Define it by origin and by who was there before the newcomers, not by length of stay: an inheemse naam is a name from the language of the people who lived in an area long before settlers came from other lands, or of the people whose language has its roots in that area. Avoid 'die eerste mense' as the definition: the Khoikhoi were not the first people at the Gariep (San hunter-gatherers were there before them), so that wording would create a new false claim."
